            11. Common Mistakes to Avoid
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Assuming every flavor is NSF certified</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Only selected flavors of Level-1, Phormula-1 and Phormula-1 Natural appear in the NSF Certified for Sport database. Birthday Cake, Maple Butter Waffle and several other Level-1 flavors are not on 1st Phorm's NSF list. Drug-tested athletes should match the exact flavor in NSF's database and look for the mark on the tub.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying Phormula-1 as a hydrolyzed whey</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Phormula-1 is a standard whey protein isolate. Its ingredient list has no hydrolyzed whey or peptides, despite the fast-absorbing marketing. That is fine for most people, since isolate digests quickly anyway, but if you specifically want a hydrolysate, Dymatize ISO100 includes one and costs less per gram on Amazon.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Using Level-1 as a lactose-free option</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Level-1 is built on whey concentrate and milk protein concentrate, so every flavor carries lactose, and 1st Phorm says plainly that it is not low in lactose. If dairy sugar upsets your stomach, Phormula-1 has only trace lactose, and Phormula-1 Clear is the brand's lactose-free option.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Comparing price per tub instead of per gram</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                A $62.99 tub of Level-1 looks similar to a 2 lb tub of other whey, but it holds only 690 g of protein. Divide the price by servings times protein, then by 25. At list price, 1st Phorm runs about $2.19 to $2.54 per 25 g, against about $1.49 for Gold Standard.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Pouring Level-1 straight into hot coffee</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                1st Phorm warns that adding Level-1 directly to piping hot liquid makes it clump, and its milk proteins thicken quickly. Let the coffee cool for a few minutes, or mix the scoop into two ounces of cold milk or water first and pour the coffee in afterwards. Caramel Latte is the brand's suggested coffee flavor.
              </p>
